From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0408-mk-01-log-failed-macro-parameters.patch

Source: 0408-mk-01-log-failed-macro-parameters.patch
capped

Run85 (Mario Kart World, T23 env) is the only run of 125 with failed macros: 150 lines
"Native MME (JIT) failed: start=0x1e6, consumed=6/6, error=instruction limit exceeded" from
62.8 s, two of start=0x21a, and between them draws skipped for counts that decode as floats.
The app was gone 11 s later with no report. The line says nothing about what the macro was
given, so it cannot tell a macro fed garbage from a macro that runs a wrong loop.

FailedMacroParameters() in macro.cpp adds ", parameters=<hex words>" (at most 64) to the three
failure lines that lacked them: the JIT and the interpreter in MacroEngine::Execute, and the
split front's JIT in maxwell_3d.cpp, where fs.parameters still holds the call's words because
the JIT reads them in place. Capped at 16 failures per start address and 128 in all; the plain
line continues after. The compute engine's line already carried its parameters. No switch: a
failed macro is already an error line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
